{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_86","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('tests/check.py');s=p.read_text().replace('            guest.wait_for_timeout(500)\\\\n            require(\\\\n                host.evaluate(\\\"__DE.game.width\\\") < 3,\\\\n                \\\"formation does not fit a phone guest\\\",\\\\n            )','            host.wait_for_function(\\\"__DE.game.width < 3\\\", timeout=10000)\\\\n            metrics[\\\"directLink\\\"][\\\"guestWidth\\\"]=guest.evaluate(\\\"__DE.app.view.width\\\")\\\\n            metrics[\\\"directLink\\\"][\\\"hostWidth\\\"]=host.evaluate(\\\"__DE.game.width\\\")')\ns=s.replace('                \\\"guest could not return to solo\\\",\\\\n            )','                \\\"guest could not return to solo\\\",\\\\n            )\\\\n            host.wait_for_function(\\\"__DE.game.players[1].left === true\\\",timeout=10000)')\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('feedback.json');r=json.loads(p.read_text());r['sourceInformation']['testing']='37 grouped automated checks: deterministic Rapier collisions and a full seven-encounter AI playthrough, offline WebGPU startup, keyboard/mouse, standard gamepad emulation, phone touch, audio sample analysis, real two-page WebRTC, and four AI Hub scenarios including 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter, 5% loss, host departure and a host without a player seat. Visual and four-copy stress checks use the same renderer’s WebGL 2 backend. Physical hardware, human listening and WAN NAT traversal are unknown.'\nr['sourceInformation']['research']='No source or general internet research; native model knowledge only. Read the user-supplied AI Hub protocol and pinned dependency source for implementation; no internet search.'\nr['testingFeedback']=[\n '5 game issues found and fixed: inline-script packaging, missed brief ability taps, phone-title overflow, HUD overlap and renderer startup recovery. Three test-runner/fixture issues were also corrected.',\n '2 blocked play in affected builds or environments: broken inline-script packaging and failed renderer initialization.',\n 'The seeded full-game AI playthrough using real Rapier collisions. It completed every encounter, all enemy mechanics, both boss transitions, pickups, dashes and Encores; the Hub harness separately checked multiplayer lifecycle.',\n 'Software WebGPU screenshots were least useful: canvas capture was blank despite active simulation and renderer frames. The same scenes captured through the WebGL 2 backend were useful for composition.'\n]\nr['engineFeedback']=[\n 'Three.js TSL supplied consistent quantized lighting across procedural models; AnimationMixer made reusable wingbeats and thrusters straightforward.',\n 'Brief input polling and minified-script embedding initially needed corrections. Software WebGPU startup across many iframe lifetimes required recovery through the renderer’s WebGL 2 backend; state checks were more reliable than WebGPU screenshots.',\n 'The fixed-step gameplay simulation, controller-first UI and host-authoritative co-op, including standalone pairing and the Hub lifecycle.',\n 'Coordinating asynchronous renderer startup, native animation, Rapier sensor collisions and network snapshots across local, remote and headless-authority roles.',\n 'none',\n 'Built-in device-loss recovery with actionable renderer startup diagnostics.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nbiome check --write src build.mjs tests/physics.mjs package.json feedback.json biome.json --diagnostic-level=error\nruff check tests/check.py\nruff format tests/check.py\nnpm test\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
